sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Desktop
    participant Mobile
    participant API
    participant DB as Database
    
    Note over User,DB: Device 1: Desktop Login
    User->>Desktop: Login with NOSTR pubkey
    Desktop->>API: POST /api/unified-sessions/create
    API->>DB: Check existing sessions count
    DB-->>API: 2 active sessions
    API->>DB: Insert new session (device_id: desktop_123)
    API->>DB: Log activity: login
    API-->>Desktop: Session + Token (device 3 of 5)
    Desktop->>User: Login successful
    
    Note over User,DB: Device 2: Mobile Login (Same User)
    User->>Mobile: Login with same NOSTR pubkey
    Mobile->>API: POST /api/unified-sessions/create
    API->>DB: Check existing sessions count
    DB-->>API: 3 active sessions
    API->>DB: Insert new session (device_id: mobile_456)
    API->>DB: Log activity: login
    API-->>Mobile: Session + Token (device 4 of 5)
    Mobile->>User: Login successful
    
    Note over User,DB: Concurrent Usage
    Desktop->>API: POST /api/unified-sessions/validate
    API->>DB: Validate desktop session
    DB-->>API: Valid, update last_activity
    API-->>Desktop: Session valid
    
    Mobile->>API: POST /api/unified-sessions/validate
    API->>DB: Validate mobile session
    DB-->>API: Valid, update last_activity
    API-->>Mobile: Session valid
    
    Note over User,DB: Session Limit Enforcement
    User->>Desktop: Login on NEW device (6th device)
    Desktop->>API: POST /api/unified-sessions/create
    API->>DB: Check existing sessions count
    DB-->>API: 5 active sessions (AT LIMIT)
    API->>DB: Revoke OLDEST session
    API->>DB: Insert new session
    API-->>Desktop: Session created (oldest revoked)
    
    Note over User,DB: Device-Specific Revocation
    User->>Desktop: Revoke mobile device
    Desktop->>API: DELETE /api/unified-sessions/revoke-device
    API->>DB: Mark mobile sessions inactive
    DB-->>API: 2 sessions revoked
    API-->>Desktop: Mobile sessions revoked
    
    Mobile->>API: POST /api/unified-sessions/validate
    API->>DB: Check session status
    DB-->>API: Session inactive
    API-->>Mobile: Session invalid (401)
    Mobile->>User: Please log in again
